<title>INDONESIA: Matahari revises down 1996 net target.</title>
<headline>Matahari revises down 1996 net target.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesian department store operator PT Matahari Putra Prima said on Tuesday that it had revised down its 1996 net profit target.</p>
<p>Matahari's finance director, Hanifah Komala, said they revised down net profit for 1996 to 46 billion from its original target of 50 billion rupiah.</p>
<p>&quot;We have to revised down our target due to weak sales performance in the third quarter,&quot; said Komala.</p>
<p>He also said the company expect to record a 83 billion rupiah of net profit in 1997.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364</p>
</text>
